## How to read this

AF29 asks for one place that keeps four kinds of status apart. A row moves right only with evidence for that column.

|Column|Means|Evidence needed|
|-|-|-|
|Source|The behavior exists in the code|A path in the repository|
|Tested|A test exercises the behavior, including an adverse case where one matters|A named test that passed in the recorded run|
|Released|A tagged release ships it|A tag. The 3.1.0 train is not a release|
|Study|A study result bears on it|A pilot or confirmatory result in this repository. Harness fixtures never count|

`partial` means some of the requirement is met, and the row says which part. Update a row when its status changes, and record the commit.

:::agent Matrix rules
- Never mark a column without the evidence its definition asks for. Code presence is not a test, a passing test is not a release, and a harness run on the fixture is not study evidence.
- When a row changes, update `updated` and the run record below.
:::

