|C02|`test/bench/netTokens.ts` reads files at their own path, passes `--today`, takes full or outline from `smd read`, records commit, CLI hash, Node and OS|`implementationReview.test.ts` (relative include, fixed date, both readers)|Partly|3.1.0 train (`docs/TOKENS.md` re-run)|Failure on a CLI error, the run record's contents and `--reader` validation are untested|
|C03|`test/eval/` (corpus validator, conditions M1–O and four ablations, survival check, scorer with paired bootstrap)|`eval.test.ts` (about 25 tests, CLI end to end)|Yes (broken ids, spans, evidence, violations, superseded options)|3.1.0 train|The corpus `research/corpus/` does not exist. Only the fixture, which is not study data. M2 and S3 are oracle renders, not model-selected|
